From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:21:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 522/528] [DS4.1] MXFP4-CSF leaves the DS4.1 package; Kimi and
 DS4-Flash keep its experts

vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/mxfp4_csf.py held two things: the MXFP4-CSF
routed-expert method (Mxfp4CsfMoEMethod, B12X's prepared fused MoE over
losslessly compressed MXFP4 scales), which the Kimi-K3 and DeepSeek-V4-Flash
CSF configurations also use, and DeepSeek-V4.1's CSF configuration. The
recipe serves the native DS4.1 checkpoint, and DS4.1 runs TileLang kernels
only, so its CSF configuration (B12X experts inside the TileLang model) is
not served.

- The method moves, unchanged, to vllm/model_executor/layers/quantization/
  mxfp4_csf_moe.py; Kimi and DS4-Flash import it from there.
- DeepseekV41Mxfp4CsfConfig goes; the mxfp4_csf dispatcher refuses a DS4.1
  CSF checkpoint by name instead of building one.
- The CSF reader keeps its DS4.1 family contract (loader-level, unchanged).

Tests: the method's tests take DS4-Flash's CSF configuration as owner; the
DS4.1 configuration's selection test goes (DS4-Flash's equivalent stays);
the dispatcher selects Kimi and refuses DS4.1.
